libdrm-phoenix 0002: xf86drm.c: Phoenix backend hooks; open_memstream fallback

- drmIoctl(): on __phoenix__ every request goes to drm_phoenix_ioctl(), which
  marshals it to the node's userspace server (rpi4-kms / rpi4-v3d-async).
- drmWaitVBlank() is the one public entry that calls ioctl() directly instead
  of drmIoctl(); on __phoenix__ it goes through drmIoctl() like every other.
- Device identity (no sysfs, no DRM major): drmGetDevices2, drmGetDevice2,
  drmGetDeviceFromDevId, drmGetNodeTypeFromDevId, drmGetNodeTypeFromFd,
  drmGetDeviceNameFromFd[2], drmGetMinorNameForFD (-> drmGet{Primary,Render}-
  DeviceNameFromFd) and drmOpenMinor (-> drmOpen*, drmAvailable) each gain one
  __phoenix__ branch calling the backend (xf86drm_phoenix.h).
- meson already computes HAVE_OPEN_MEMSTREAM but nothing checked it: without
  open_memstream the two format-modifier name printers now fail soft (they
  return NULL on any open_memstream failure already) instead of not compiling.
Base: upstream libdrm b97cbde. MIT.

